/accounts shows the banner visible, the region holding the real warning
text (not "dismissed"), and sessionStorage empty.

POINTS 7/12 (contrast) — PASS, re-measured from scratch in both themes.
Fixed a compositing bug in my own instrument (was compositing translucent
backgrounds against pure white instead of accumulating all ancestor
layers) before trusting the numbers; cross-checked every figure against
axe-core's color-contrast rule scoped directly to #accounts-warnings-banner
(0 violations, light theme).
  LIGHT: explanatory <p class="text-xs ... text-amber-700">, the dismiss
    button, and the "Pattern overlap warning" heading span are all
    rgb(180,83,9) (amber-700) on a fully-opaque composited rgb(255,251,235)
    background = 4.842:1 — passes the 4.5:1 body-text floor (matches the
    worker's and attempt-2's independently-reproduced figure exactly).
  DARK: explanatory text and dismiss button are rgb(251,191,36) (amber-400)
    on a composited ~rgb(48,33,32) background = 9.249:1; the heading span
    (amber-300, rgb(252,211,77)) = 10.708:1. Both comfortably clear 4.5:1.
    (The composited dark background differs numerically from attempt-2's
    figure because attempt-2's own compositing likely had the same
    single-white-layer flaw I found and fixed in mine; the class list
    driving these colors — bg-amber-900/30, text-amber-400 — is unchanged
    by this diff, and the margin here is wide enough that the exact
    ancestor stack does not change the verdict.)

POINT 9 (visible focus indicator) — PASS.
With the dismiss button focused via real Tab navigation, computed style
shows `outline: rgba(0,0,0,0) solid 2px` (a transparent outline, i.e. the
